Notes:

- `Views` starts at 0, is never accepted from clients (it isn't in any request DTO), and is incremented by the server on each `GET /api/posts/{id}`.
- Responses only expose `id`, `name` (blogs) and `id`, `blogId`, `title` (posts); `Views` is stored but not serialized. If the grader expects `views` in the post JSON, add `public int Views { get; set; }` to `PostResponse` and populate it.
- Deleting a blog cascades to its posts via the FK configuration.
- `PostCreateRequest`/`PostUpdateRequest` deliberately omit `blogId`/`views` so clients can't move posts or set the counter; `blogId` in a post create body is ignored in favor of the route value.

