Notes on the design:

- Entities are named exactly `Blog` and `Post`; `Post.Views` is server-maintained — initialized to 0 on create, never read from the request body, and incremented on each `GET /api/posts/{id}` (the most natural interpretation of a view counter). I also exposed the same incrementing GET on `BlogsController` via an absolute route so both paths work.
- `PUT` updates only mutable fields (`Name`, `Title`); ids and `Views` are untouched.
- JSON is camelCase by default in ASP.NET Core; GUIDs bind automatically in routes and bodies.
- `AppSetup.ConfigureServices` registers the `DbContext` with the provided SQLite connection string. Controllers and `AddControllers()` are left to the grader as specified.

