Notes:

- `Post.Views` is incremented on `GET /api/posts/{id}` and ignored on writes, so clients can never set it.
- POSTs accept an optional client-supplied `id`; retries with the same id return the already-created resource instead of failing on a duplicate key, and a concurrent insert of the same id returns the winner.
- DELETEs are idempotent (`204` whether or not the entity existed), and `[Timestamp]` row versions make lost-update races surface as `DbUpdateConcurrencyException` (translated to `404` when the row was deleted mid-race).
- JSON is camelCase by default under `AddControllers()` with the default `System.Text.Json` options.

