Notes on the design:

- `Views` defaults to `0`, is server-maintained, and is never read from request bodies — the `PostRequest` DTO only accepts `title`, so clients can't set it (and no endpoint increments it, since the spec defines no read-tracking route; it's included in responses).
- Server generates GUIDs on create; client-supplied ids in bodies are ignored via the request DTOs.
- `GET`/`PUT`/`DELETE` on missing ids return 404; creating a post under a missing blog returns 404.
- Blog deletion cascades to its posts via the EF relationship (SQLite enforces it here since `EnsureCreated` creates the FK; EF Core's cascade delete also handles tracked orphans).
- No Program.cs or WebApplication — `AppSetup.ConfigureServices` registers only the DbContext; the grader supplies controllers and JSON config (camelCase is the ASP.NET Core default).

