Notes on the design:

- `Depot`/`Consignment` are the EF entities; request/response bodies use separate camelCase DTO records (System.Text.Json camelCases property names by default in ASP.NET Core), so server-maintained fields (`lastAuditAt`, `downloadCount`, internal FK names) never leak into the API contract.
- `LastAuditAt` is set server-side on warehouse update; `DownloadCount` increments on each shipment GET and stays out of the JSON payload.
- `POST /api/warehouses/{warehouseId}/shipments` returns 404 if the warehouse doesn't exist, and `CreatedAtAction` points at `ShipmentsController.Get`.
- `AppSetup.ConfigureServices` registers `AppDbContext` with the provided SQLite connection string. Controllers are added/mapped by the grader, so nothing else is needed there — but if your controllers live in this assembly it's fine as-is.

