Notes:

- Entities are named `Blog` and `Post`; `Post.Views` is server-maintained and incremented on each successful `GET /api/posts/{id}` (it is never accepted from clients since the request DTOs only carry `Name`/`Title`).
- Responses use camelCase by default ASP.NET Core JSON naming (`System.Text.Json` camelCase policy) — property names already match (`id`, `name`, `blogId`, `title`).
- Deleting a blog cascades to its posts via `OnDelete(DeleteBehavior.Cascade)`.
- `AppSetup.ConfigureServices` registers controllers and the `AppDbContext` bound to the given SQLite connection string; no `Program.cs` needed.
- Status codes: `201 Created` on create, `204 NoContent` on delete, `404` for missing resources, `400` for malformed bodies.

