Design notes:

- `Depot`/`Consignment` have an internal `int Key` PK, unique index on `PublicId`, `ETag` as the EF concurrency token, `CreateHash` immutable via `SetAfterSaveBehavior(Throw)`, and `DeletedAt` tombstone with a global query filter.
- Creates insert first and classify the SQLite unique violation (`SqliteErrorCode == 19`); replays are detected by comparing the stored `CreateHash`, which doubles as the "same content" check.
- Canonical JSON is built by hand with the required escaping rules, NFC normalization, lowercase GUIDs, and decimal formatting without trailing zeros; server-owned fields (`DownloadCount`, `LastAuditAt`, `DeletedAt`) never enter the hash or the response DTOs.
- PUT validates the body before checking `If-Match` (400 precedes 428), treats an unchanged body as an idempotent 204, uses optimistic concurrency on the ETag column so racing writers produce one 204 and one 412 rather than a 5xx.
- Warehouse delete tombstones its shipments in the same `SaveChangesAsync` transaction; soft-deleted rows get a fresh ETag value (not part of any representation) so stale concurrency entries never conflict.

