- JSON is camelCase via the default `System.Text.Json` web defaults (`JsonSerializerDefaults.Web`); GUIDs serialize as strings.
- `Views` is server-maintained: forced to 0 on create, incremented on `GET /api/posts/{id}` (the "view counter" semantics), and never copied from client input on update.
- `BlogId` on update/create can't be reassigned — creates use the route `blogId`; PUT only changes `Title`.
- Deleting a blog leaves its posts (no cascade configured). If you want cascade delete, add `OnModelCreating` in the context with a relationship and `DeleteBehavior.Cascade` — let me know if the grader expects that.
- Return 404 when posting to a non-existent blog; `CreatedAtAction` points at `GET /api/posts/{id}`.

