Notes on the choices made where the spec left room:

- `LastAuditAt` is set server-side on create and update; clients can't set it because `Update` only copies `Code`/`CapacityCubicMeters` (or shipment fields).
- `DownloadCount` starts at 0 and increments on each `GET /api/shipments/{id}`.
- Deleting a warehouse also deletes its consignments to keep the data consistent.
- Entities are returned directly, so JSON includes the extra `lastAuditAt`/`downloadCount` fields alongside the specified ones; ASP.NET Core's default camelCase policy produces the required property names (`capacityCubicMeters`, `warehouseId`, `weightKg`).

