Notes on choices made:

- Entities are named `Depot` and `Consignment`; JSON serializes camelCase automatically via the web defaults (`capacityCubicMeters`, `warehouseId`, `weightKg`, `downloadCount`, `lastAuditAt`).
- `LastAuditAt` is set to `DateTime.UtcNow` on warehouse create/update/read — clients can't set it since PUT only copies `Code` and `CapacityCubicMeters`.
- `DownloadCount` is server-maintained and increments on each `GET /api/shipments/{id}`.
- `WeightKg` is mapped as `TEXT` in SQLite so decimal values round-trip exactly through `EnsureCreated` (EF Core's default decimal mapping can lose precision in SQLite).
- POST returns `201 Created` with a `Location` header; PUT returns `204`; missing resources return `404`; mismatched route/body IDs return `400`.

